Formatter: the quote-flip check for nested triple-quoted literals looked at the literal's own
quote; in 3.12+ input (`f'{''''z'''}'`) the quotes oscillated between runs.
Regression test included; fuzz repro: repro/fix-formatter-fstring-nested-quote.py (ruff_formatter_idempotency).

diff --git a/crates/ruff_python_formatter/resources/test/fixtures/ruff/expression/nested_string_quote_style.py b/crates/ruff_python_formatter/resources/test/fixtures/ruff/expression/nested_string_quote_style.py
index 76657855ca32f740070256ca4a728bdf027fee67..e32f2e020ad9eae920b0ccdd68b491ca6553976f 100644
--- a/crates/ruff_python_formatter/resources/test/fixtures/ruff/expression/nested_string_quote_style.py
+++ b/crates/ruff_python_formatter/resources/test/fixtures/ruff/expression/nested_string_quote_style.py
@@ -88,3 +88,9 @@ t'{v:{d["n"]}}'
 
 # A nested f-string inside a format spec adds another level of nesting.
 f'''{v:{f"{d['n']}"}}'''
+
+# 3.12+ syntax: a nested triple-quoted literal that reuses the outer quote.
+# The quote check must look at the quote the outer f-string would get, not at the
+# nested literal's own quote, or the quotes oscillate between formatter runs.
+f'{''''z'''}'
+f"{"""'z"""}"
